---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import logo from '../assets/connected-speech-logo-transparent.png';
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Connected Speech | Speech Therapist Sandton"
  description="Meet Jodi Zimmerman, the speech-language pathologist behind Connected Speech in Sandton with over 8 years of clinical experience, specialising in AAC, Makaton, and the PROMPT system."
path="/about"
  ogTitle="About Connected Speech | Speech Therapist Sandton"
  ogDescription="Person-centred, family-first speech therapy in Sandton, built on one belief: everyone thrives when communication is consistent."
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://connectedspeech.co.za" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "About", "item": "https://connectedspeech.co.za/about" }
    ]
  }
  </script>

  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span aria-current="page">About</span>
  </nav>

  <!-- About Connected Speech -->
  <section class="section about-cs" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="about-cs-grid">
        <div class="about-cs-text">
          <span class="section-label">Who We Are</span>
          <h1 class="section-heading" id="about-heading">Built on one belief: everyone thrives when communication is consistent.</h1>
          <div class="section-body">
            <p>
              Connected Speech is a Sandton based private speech therapy practice working with children and adults
              who face communication challenges. We work with those who stutter, with
              <a href="/therapy-services/speech-therapy">language delays</a>,
              <a href="/therapy-services/feeding-therapy">feeding therapy</a>, and with
              <a href="/therapy-services/special-needs-speech-therapy">complex communication needs</a>.
            </p>
            <p>
              Communication is more than speech. Some find their voice with words. Others use signs,
              symbols, devices, or gestures, and every one of those pathways is equally valid. Our job is to
              find what works for you and build on it, in every environment where you live, learn, and grow.
            </p>
            <p>
              That means therapy does not stop when the session ends. We bring consistent, goal-driven support
              into the spaces that matter most, so progress is not left at the door.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="values-list" aria-label="Our values">
            <div class="value-item">
              <div class="value-dot" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <p><strong>Person-centred.</strong> Every therapy plan is built around the individual: their needs, their pace, their world.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="value-item">
              <div class="value-dot" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <p><strong>Inclusive by design.</strong> Communication takes many forms. We support all of them.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="value-item">
              <div class="value-dot" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <p><strong>Family-first.</strong> Families are partners in therapy, not bystanders. We make sure you know exactly how to support your loved one between sessions.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="value-item">
              <div class="value-dot" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <p><strong>Results you can see.</strong> Real progress, reported clearly, after every session.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-cs-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <Image src={logo} alt="" width={200} densities={[1, 2]} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About Jodi -->
  <section class="section about-jodi" aria-labelledby="jodi-heading">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="about-jodi-grid">
        <div class="about-jodi-text">
          <span class="section-label">Meet the Founder</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading" id="jodi-heading">Jodi Zimmerman</h2>
          <div class="section-body">
            <p>
              Jodi is a speech therapist who has spent almost a decade working with people who communicate differently, and she has never
              tired of the moment someone finds a way to be understood.
            </p>
            <p>
              After four years embedded in a government school for children with autism, Jodi developed a deep
              understanding of what people are capable of when they are given the right tools, the right
              environment, and someone who truly believes in them. That experience shaped her as a therapist
              and informed everything about how Connected Speech works today.
            </p>
            <p>
              Jodi specialises in <a href="/therapy-services/special-needs-speech-therapy">Augmentative and Alternative Communication (AAC)</a>, working with those
              whose communication goes beyond speech. Makaton signing, the PROMPT, picture-based
              communication, and high-tech devices are all part of her toolkit. She builds individualised therapy
              plans for each person, because no two people communicate in exactly the same way.
            </p>
            <p>
              Her master's dissertation explored how youth empowerment programs can facilitate participation for
              young people with disabilities, research that continues to shape her approach to therapy and her
              belief that every person deserves a seat at the table.
            </p>
            <p>
              She was selected for the Dean's List during her master's program, a reflection of the same
              commitment she brings to every person she works with.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="jodi-credentials" aria-label="Jodi's qualifications">
            <div class="credential">
              <span class="credential-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
              <span>BSc Speech-Language Pathology, University of Cape Town, 2016</span>
            </div>
            <div class="credential">
              <span class="credential-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
              <span>MSc Augmentative &amp; Alternative Communication, University of Pretoria, 2022</span>
            </div>
            <div class="credential">
              <span class="credential-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
              <span>8 years of clinical experience in speech therapy</span>
            </div>
            <div class="credential">
              <span class="credential-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
              <span>Specialist in AAC, Makaton, and PROMPT</span>
            </div>
            <div class="credential">
              <span class="credential-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
              <span>Dean's List, MSc programme, University of Pretoria</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-section" aria-labelledby="about-cta-heading">
    <div class="cta-grid">
      <div class="cta-grid-text">
        <h2 id="about-cta-heading">You have something to say.<br/>Let's help you say it.</h2>
        <p>
          We work with families and individuals across Sandton, Johannesburg. Our therapist is available
          Monday to Thursday. Sessions are billed through medical aid and cash.
        </p>
        <p class="cta-note">Medical aid and cash accepted.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-grid-form">
        <ContactForm dark />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
